# mcp-mrtr-elicit-roundtrip - ze_execute asks for the missing command through a
# Multi Round-Trip Request, the client answers on a retry, the command runs.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-mcp2026-2-mrtr AC-1 and AC-2, and end-to-end user story 1.
# The first probe shows the interim result verbatim: resultType
# "input_required", one inputRequests entry whose value is an elicitation/create
# request carrying an explicit "mode":"form" -- and NO requestState, which is
# what makes the exchange stateless. The directive that follows then drives the
# real round trip: the client constructs the input, retries the ORIGINAL request
# under a new JSON-RPC id with inputResponses, and the dispatched command's
# output (the configured peer name) reaches stdout.
#
# WHAT CHANGED AND WHY: this replaces elicitation-accept.ci, which proved the
# same user outcome through the mechanism MCP 2026-07-28 deleted -- a POST
# upgraded to SSE, a server-initiated elicitation/create JSON-RPC request, and a
# correlated client JSON-RPC response. The transport now forbids both halves of
# that exchange, so the old test could only pass against a non-conformant
# server. The outcome asserted is unchanged; the protocol carrying it is not.
#
# PREVENTS: the interim result being labelled "complete" (a client would read a
# prompt as an answer), the mode field being dropped (which hides the url-mode
# gap), a requestState appearing (umbrella R-3, a signed-but-unbound replay
# primitive), and the retry failing to merge the answer into the dispatch.

stdin=mcp:terminator=EOF_MCP
wait-peers
probe tools/call {"name":"ze_execute","arguments":{}}
elicit-answer accept show bgp peer list
@ze_execute {}
EOF_MCP

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze --mcp $PORT -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test mcp --port $PORT --elicit form:stdin=mcp:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
# The interim result, in full. pattern= rather than contains= because every
# needle carries a colon and a contains= value is split on it (ci.ParseKVPairs).
expect=stdout:pattern="resultType":"input_required"
expect=stdout:contains=inputRequests
expect=stdout:contains=elicitation/create
expect=stdout:pattern="mode":"form"
expect=stdout:pattern="requestedSchema"
# It is an interim SUCCESS, not a tool error: HTTP 200, code=ok, no isError.
expect=stdout:pattern=probe status=200 code=ok
# The retry ran the answered command: the configured peer is in the output.
expect=stdout:contains=peer1
# No requestState anywhere. Ze mints none, so any occurrence is either a server
# emitting state it cannot verify later or a client inventing one.
reject=stdout:contains=requestState
# The server never writes a JSON-RPC request frame. AC-3's first half: an
# elicitation/create is a plain {method, params} OBJECT nested in inputRequests,
# never a message of its own, so no JSON-RPC envelope may appear anywhere in a
# printed result.
#
# This replaces `"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":[0-9]+,"method":"elicitation/create"`,
# which could not match whatever the server did: formatProbeResult
# (internal/test/cli/cmd_mcp.go) prints the frame's `result` MEMBER, never the
# enclosing frame, so no line of this client's stdout is ever shaped like a
# whole JSON-RPC message. The needle below is inside that printed member, so it
# fires the moment newElicitRequest (internal/component/mcp/elicit.go) starts
# building a frame instead of an object.
reject=stdout:pattern="jsonrpc":"2\.0"
# AC-15's interim half (spec-mcp2026-4-caching-apps): an input_required result
# "is not cacheable and carries no caching hints". The probe above prints the
# whole interim result, so a hint stamped onto it would land here. tools/list is
# never called in this run, so neither key has any other way to reach stdout.
reject=stdout:pattern="ttlMs"
reject=stdout:pattern="cacheScope"
